module extdeps.ampere.mt_collins_product_brief.bmc

import std.types { String }
import extdeps.bmc.endpoint { BmcFirmwareFamily, AmiMegaRac }
import extdeps.ampere.mt_collins_product_brief.subject { MtCollinsPublicProductBrief, mt_collins_public_product_brief }
import extdeps.external_authority { ExternalAuthority }
import extdeps.uri { Uri, Https }

data extdeps_external_authority_anchor: ExternalAuthority = ExternalAuthority {
  uri: Uri {
    scheme: Https,
    locator: "amperecomputing.com/customer-connect/products/mt-collins",
  }
}

data bmc_subject: MtCollinsPublicProductBrief = mt_collins_public_product_brief

// The management stack a workflow holding a Foxconn Mt. Collins should EXPECT: AMI
// MegaRAC, reached over IPMI lanplus and the proprietary REST surface modeled in
// extdeps.bmc.megarac. The expectation traces to one unpreserved operator run on
// 2026-08-29, recorded below as unverified historical report; it is confirmed or
// contradicted only by an intake receipt from an attempt against the unit. Factory login
// and API contract rows live with the stack (extdeps.bmc.megarac), not here - this row
// only binds platform to expected family so a workflow knows which access authority to
// try first.
type MtCollinsBmcImplementationExpected {
  family: BmcFirmwareFamily
}

data mt_collins_bmc_implementation_expected: MtCollinsBmcImplementationExpected = MtCollinsBmcImplementationExpected { family: AmiMegaRac }

data mt_collins_bmc_expectation_provenance_note: String = "EXPECTATION, NOT AN UPSTREAM FACT (machine-intake ruling 2026-08-29 §1, on gunbc#9690). This module's external authority is Ampere's public product page, which does not state the BMC firmware product; the family here was established by one operator execution against one held unit, which is an OBSERVATION, and an observation rendered as an extdeps row is the provenance inversion DESIGN §3 names. So the row is typed as what it is — what a workflow holding a Mt. Collins should EXPECT to find — and the observation that would confirm or contradict it is a workflow-layer gunbc.machine_intake_access BmcImplementationObserved receipt keyed to unit, attempt, endpoint, time and raw Manager-response evidence. No such receipt is authored yet: the raw producer output of the 2026-08-29 run (Manager Manufacturer/Model/FirmwareVersion payload, both VirtualMedia discovery routes, service roster) was not preserved, and the ruling forbids seeding it from memory. The two rows below (mt_collins_bmc_unverified_historical_report_no_redfish, mt_collins_bmc_unverified_historical_report_provenance) are the only record of that run, and they are unverified operator report: historical, not observation, and not fallback authority for any workflow."

data mt_collins_bmc_unverified_historical_report_no_redfish: String = "UNVERIFIED HISTORICAL OPERATOR REPORT, NOT AN OBSERVATION (machine-intake ruling 3, gunbc#9690). An operator reported on 2026-08-29 that on one held unit GET /redfish/v1 returned 404, that the firmware self-reported as `0.32`, and that the service roster was web/kvm/cd-media/hd-media/ssh with no Redfish service. The raw producer output of that run was not preserved, so nothing here is grounded by execution: no receipt, no unit key, no attempt identity, no response bytes. It is retained only as the historical record of what was reported, so the next intake attempt knows what it is expected to confirm or contradict. No workflow may read this row as an observation, as a build-grain protocol fact, or as any kind of authority; the only carrier that can state what the unit's BMC actually answers is a workflow-layer intake receipt produced by an attempt against the unit."

data mt_collins_bmc_unverified_historical_report_provenance: String = "UNVERIFIED HISTORICAL OPERATOR REPORT, NOT AN OBSERVATION. The public Ampere/Foxconn documents for Mt. Collins do not state the BMC firmware product; the AMI MegaRAC expectation in this module traces to the same unpreserved 2026-08-29 operator run and to nothing else. A re-flashed unit would carry a different implementation than expected - and as of 2026-08-29 no OpenBMC machine layer exists for Mt. Collins (upstream and Ampere-fork meta-ampere carry meta-jade, meta-jefferson and meta-mitchell only; an OpenBMC Collins would be a porting project, not a flash) - which is why the implementation is typed as an EXPECTATION to be confirmed per unit, never as a default. No workflow may fall back to this module for an unprobed unit: an unprobed unit has no BMC implementation fact, and the fail-closed answer is to refuse until an intake attempt produces the receipt."
